1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,390
Welcome back to Lesson 4.4, Documenting the Monthly Clinical Review.

2
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,333
This is Part 2 of 2: Resources and Support,

3
00:00:09,383 --> 00:00:12,424
and Other Provider and Appointment Notes.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,926
In Part 1, you posted Allergies, Medications, and Numbers to Track.

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:21,633
Now you'll finish the clinical review.

6
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,147
Resources and Support: the patient's mobility,

7
00:00:25,197 --> 00:00:29,231
falls, and medical equipment, from the latest MDS.

8
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:30,290
Other Provider

9
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:34,373
and Appointment Notes: signed provider visits from the last 30 days,

10
00:00:34,423 --> 00:00:36,434
and upcoming appointments.

11
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,845
Then, you'll mark the clinical review as reviewed.

12
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:45,340
The next section is Resources and Support.

13
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,743
Here, you report two things.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,258
First, the patient's mobility: can they walk on their own, and how far?

15
00:00:52,308 --> 00:00:54,457
And have they had any falls?

16
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:59,105
Second, the durable medical equipment, or DME, the patient uses,

17
00:00:59,155 --> 00:01:03,197
such as a wheelchair, a walker, a cane, or crutches.

18
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:07,788
You'll find both in the patient's MDS, in PointClickCare.

19
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,719
In PointClickCare, open the resident's MDS tab.

20
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,821
MDS stands for Minimum Data Set.

21
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:21,847
It's an assessment the facility completes for each resident at least every quarter,

22
00:01:21,897 --> 00:01:23,619
or every three months.

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:26,207
It covers basic functions: mobility,

24
00:01:26,257 --> 00:01:31,420
and activities of daily living such as eating, showering, and toileting.

25
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:37,400
It also covers mood, with the PHQ-9 score for depression, and cognition.

26
00:01:37,667 --> 00:01:42,004
The tab lists the patient's MDS assessments, newest first.

27
00:01:42,267 --> 00:01:46,758
Use the most recent one with the status Accepted or Completed.

28
00:01:57,467 --> 00:02:00,022
To open an assessment, use View or Print.

29
00:02:00,072 --> 00:02:01,539
Here, use Print.

30
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,618
In the print options, select MDS Form, and click Print.

31
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,564
The full MDS form opens.

32
00:02:14,614 --> 00:02:16,575
It has many pages.

33
00:02:16,833 --> 00:02:18,534
Start with mobility.

34
00:02:21,367 --> 00:02:24,395
Press Control F, and search for: walk 10.

35
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:27,883
This finds the walking items: walk 10 feet,

36
00:02:27,933 --> 00:02:31,952
walk 50 feet with two turns, and walk 150 feet.

37
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:37,336
The first match isn't coded,

38
00:02:37,386 --> 00:02:40,959
so keep searching until you reach the section that is.

39
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:44,977
Here, all three distances are coded 04.

40
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,262
What does 04 mean?

41
00:02:53,312 --> 00:02:55,177
Check the coding key.

42
00:02:55,433 --> 00:03:00,995
06 means independent: the resident completes the activity with no help.

43
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:08,195
Any lower code, such as 05, 04, or 03, means the patient needs some help.

44
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:20,440
So, coded 04 for all three distances, this patient needs assistance to walk.

45
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:25,575
Each mobility case has a fixed template,

46
00:03:25,625 --> 00:03:28,970
in the CCM Clinical Tool, under Templates.

47
00:03:32,767 --> 00:03:35,203
Needs assistance in all 3: use it when

48
00:03:35,253 --> 00:03:39,432
the patient needs assistance in all three walk distances.

49
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,899
If the patient can't walk 10 feet without help,

50
00:03:42,949 --> 00:03:46,164
they can't manage 50 or 150 feet either.

51
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:48,830
It reads: The patient has significant

52
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:51,806
difficulty with ambulation and moving around.

53
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:55,310
They are not able to walk without assistance, and do,

54
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,852
or do not, experience falls or balance issues.

55
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:12,199
No issues: use it when the patient is independent,

56
00:04:12,249 --> 00:04:15,173
coded 06, in all three distances.

57
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:22,909
Some difficulty: use it when the patient isn't independent in all three,

58
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:27,924
for example 06 for 10 feet, but lower for the longer distances.

59
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:31,934
No recent MDS evaluation: use it when no new

60
00:04:31,984 --> 00:04:36,219
MDS was done after the last date of service.

61
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:41,461
Independent

62
00:04:41,511 --> 00:04:46,402
but falls: use it when the patient is independent in all three distances,

63
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:47,849
but has falls.

64
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,857
Also note: reading glasses aren't DME.

65
00:04:50,907 --> 00:04:55,938
Instead, write: Patient uses over the counter reading glasses.

66
00:05:05,567 --> 00:05:10,053
For this patient, the right template is: needs assistance in all 3.

67
00:05:12,233 --> 00:05:15,582
The template also says whether the patient has falls.

68
00:05:15,632 --> 00:05:17,749
Check that in the MDS too.

69
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,257
Search for: falls.

70
00:05:21,567 --> 00:05:26,609
Find Any Falls Since Admission, Entry or Reentry, or Prior Assessment.

71
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:28,951
0 means no, and 1 means yes.

72
00:05:29,001 --> 00:05:32,881
Here it's 0, so the patient has had no falls.

73
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:40,727
Back in the CCM Clinical Tool, click Copy on the template.

74
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:48,595
In ThoroughCare, click Add Update, in Resources and Support Notes.

75
00:05:49,067 --> 00:05:50,571
Paste the template.

76
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:53,130
Then fix the do, or do not, part.

77
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:54,978
This patient has no falls,

78
00:05:55,028 --> 00:05:59,388
so it reads: do not experience falls or balance issues.

79
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,911
Next, the equipment.

80
00:06:01,961 --> 00:06:04,238
Start a new line for DME.

81
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:08,327
In the MDS, search for: walker.

82
00:06:09,933 --> 00:06:15,785
This finds Mobility Devices: the devices normally used in the last 7 days.

83
00:06:16,267 --> 00:06:19,802
Cane or crutch, walker, wheelchair, or limb prosthesis.

84
00:06:19,852 --> 00:06:22,910
Here, walker and wheelchair are checked.

85
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:27,061
Then search for: glasses.

86
00:06:29,267 --> 00:06:33,654
Corrective lenses are coded 0, so the patient doesn't use them.

87
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:42,614
Back in ThoroughCare, type: DMEs: Patient uses a walker and a wheelchair.

88
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,397
Then click Save.

89
00:06:45,667 --> 00:06:48,372
The Resources and Support note is saved.

90
00:06:49,967 --> 00:06:53,541
The last section is Other Provider and Appointment Notes.

91
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,072
Here, you document two things.

92
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:56,680
First,

93
00:06:56,730 --> 00:07:01,379
every provider visit from the last 30 days that the provider documented

94
00:07:01,429 --> 00:07:02,607
and signed.

95
00:07:02,867 --> 00:07:07,598
You follow up on the patient every month, so you cover the last 30 days.

96
00:07:07,867 --> 00:07:12,945
Second, any upcoming appointments, lab tests, or diagnostic tests.

97
00:07:20,967 --> 00:07:25,644
Provider visits are in PointClickCare, in the resident's progress notes.

98
00:07:25,694 --> 00:07:27,195
Open PROG NOTES.

99
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:35,780
At the top left, check that you're in Progress Notes, not Practitioner Notes.

100
00:07:36,033 --> 00:07:37,333
Click View All.

101
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,703
Then set the view to show the last 30 days.

102
00:07:49,333 --> 00:07:50,780
Next, search the notes.

103
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:53,362
You only document signed visits.

104
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:57,393
A signed visit means a provider saw the patient for a reason,

105
00:07:57,443 --> 00:08:01,079
documented the visit, and signed it electronically.

106
00:08:02,567 --> 00:08:04,486
So search for: signed.

107
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,786
Here's one.

108
00:08:06,836 --> 00:08:11,053
The date of service is October 12, 2026.

109
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:22,379
Scroll down to the Diagnosis, Assessment and Plan section.

110
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:26,435
It shows the conditions the provider reviewed, and the plan.

111
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:32,894
Here: mild depression, generalized anxiety disorder,

112
00:08:32,944 --> 00:08:38,028
pseudobulbar affect, and dementia, with the medications to continue.

113
00:08:42,667 --> 00:08:46,608
At the end of the note are the provider's name, and the signed date.

114
00:08:46,867 --> 00:08:51,674
Copy the provider's name, the date of service, and the Assessment and Plan.

115
00:09:02,433 --> 00:09:07,369
Visits are documented with a fixed template, in the CCM Clinical Tool.

116
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:11,414
Under Templates, open Progress Notes.

117
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:15,269
Its tip: add only signed notes with an assessment and plan,

118
00:09:15,319 --> 00:09:20,163
or recommendations, from the last date of service up to your follow-up.

119
00:09:20,433 --> 00:09:24,961
The template reads: The patient was seen by, provider name and specialty,

120
00:09:25,011 --> 00:09:28,533
on, date of service, and the plan was as follows.

121
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:29,930
Copy it.

122
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,429
On the same page,

123
00:09:31,479 --> 00:09:36,171
the DMEs template notes where DME comes from: the care profile,

124
00:09:36,221 --> 00:09:40,434
or the most recent MDS if there's no care profile.

125
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:48,706
In ThoroughCare, click Add Update, in Other Provider and Appointment Notes.

126
00:09:49,167 --> 00:09:50,671
Paste the template.

127
00:09:55,967 --> 00:10:00,039
Fill in the provider's name and specialty, and the date of service.

128
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,640
Here, the specialty was left out.

129
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:06,545
Always include it, for example: Dawn Kopp, FNP.

130
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,907
Then paste the Assessment and Plan below it.

131
00:10:10,167 --> 00:10:12,700
Document every signed visit from the last

132
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:16,413
30 days that's related to the patient's conditions.

133
00:10:19,233 --> 00:10:22,743
Back in the progress notes, check the other signed matches.

134
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,623
Here, there's no other signed provider visit.

135
00:10:25,673 --> 00:10:29,211
If there were, you'd document each one the same way.

136
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:39,068
Next, the second part of this section: upcoming appointments,

137
00:10:39,118 --> 00:10:43,947
lab tests, and diagnostic tests, such as an X-ray or an MRI.

138
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:48,975
For example, the patient may be scheduled to see a cardiologist next week.

139
00:10:53,467 --> 00:10:56,846
They're in PointClickCare, in the resident's Orders tab.

140
00:10:56,896 --> 00:10:59,427
It lists all the patient's orders.

141
00:11:03,433 --> 00:11:06,306
Open Display Filters to narrow the list.

142
00:11:10,933 --> 00:11:15,035
Under Order Category, keep only Laboratory, Diagnostic, and Other.

143
00:11:15,085 --> 00:11:17,359
Appointments are under Other.

144
00:11:18,833 --> 00:11:20,325
Then click Search.

145
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:28,429
Here's an upcoming appointment: a follow-up with Dr.

146
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:33,610
Conner, an orthopedic doctor, one time only, at 1:00 PM.

147
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:36,144
Copy it exactly as it's written.

148
00:11:44,067 --> 00:11:47,562
A tip for finding upcoming orders: double-click the Start

149
00:11:47,612 --> 00:11:50,922
Date column header to sort the orders by date.

150
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:57,733
You only need what's still to come, after today.

151
00:11:57,783 --> 00:12:02,936
Today is October 23, so only the October 27 appointment counts.

152
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:14,807
Nothing else is scheduled after it, so there's nothing more to add.

153
00:12:19,767 --> 00:12:23,310
Paste it in the same Other Provider and Appointment Notes update,

154
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,694
under the visit.

155
00:12:24,967 --> 00:12:29,647
Document any upcoming lab or diagnostic test the same way.

156
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,430
Then click Save.

157
00:12:32,567 --> 00:12:37,755
The note is saved, and every section of the clinical review is now documented.

158
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:46,588
Scroll to the bottom of the page, and click Mark as Reviewed.

159
00:12:46,867 --> 00:12:51,276
A confirmation opens, with today's date as the clinical review date.

160
00:12:51,326 --> 00:12:52,497
Click Save.

161
00:12:53,667 --> 00:12:54,925
To recap.

162
00:12:55,200 --> 00:13:00,029
For Resources and Support, open the latest Accepted or Completed MDS,

163
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:02,580
and check the walking scores.

164
00:13:02,833 --> 00:13:06,840
Post the matching mobility template, with or without falls.

165
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,599
Add the DME the patient uses.

166
00:13:09,867 --> 00:13:12,247
For Other Provider and Appointment Notes,

167
00:13:12,297 --> 00:13:17,074
document each signed visit from the last 30 days with the visit template.

168
00:13:17,333 --> 00:13:22,534
Add upcoming appointments, labs, and diagnostic tests from the Orders tab.

169
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:26,673
Save each note, then mark the clinical review as reviewed.

170
00:13:29,133 --> 00:13:31,740
That's the end of Lesson 4.4.

171
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,843
You can now document a complete monthly clinical review.
